--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8ef4a382a350f98438c21cfd3c789fdf, type: 3}
  m_Name: Ladder
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lessonTitle: Ladder
  lessonId: ladder
  slides:
  - slideName: Slide 1
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: In this lesson, you will learn how to "ladder" your opponents' stones.
      This technique is considered to be the most basic by many.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 2
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: To ladder a group of stones means to constantly put it in Atari in
      a zigzag pattern until it reaches the edge or your own stones, where it runs
      out of liberties.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 3
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: 'For example, white went at the highlighted location. Try to save your
      stones. (Hint: You won''t be able to!)'
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: c3175c4a7cb1dea4fa49251edf6f7d02, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 4
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Notice how you were constantly in Atari and couldn't escape? This is
      the power of laddering. Also, you made a zigzag pattern!
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 5
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: Try it yourself now. Get your revenge and ladder white!
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: bf00f427d8093284fa34d7139203985c, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 6
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Good job on your revenge. Laddering is indeed powerful, but if you
      use it at the wrong time or direction, your opponent might escape, and you
      will be left with a lot of weak points. (We will learn about weak points in
      a future lesson, but just know that they are very bad for you for now.)
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 7
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Take a look at this situation. Here, laddering white is possible, but
      there are other white stones in the way.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 8
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Black tries to ladder, but white escapes and connects with other stones
      (numbers indicate order of play). The other direction will have the same result.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 9
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: This is another example. Black can try to ladder white here, but notice
      how the black stones on the side are low on liberties (highlighted).
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 10
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: When black tries to ladder upwards, the upper two black stones are
      in Atari as white is escaping. If black continues to ladder at the triangle
      highlight, white will capture the two black stones by placing at the square
      highlight.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 11
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Black can only give up laddering and let white escape.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 12
    slideType: 2
    bodyText: Now it's your turn. Can black ladder the highlighted white stones successfully?
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 0
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 13
    slideType: 2
    bodyText: Can black ladder the highlighted white stones successfully now?
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 14
    slideType: 3
    bodyText: 'Which direction?

      1. Left

      2. Right'
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 1
  - slideName: Slide 15
    slideType: 2
    bodyText: Can black ladder the highlighted white stones successfully?
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 16
    slideType: 3
    bodyText: 'Which direction?

      1. Up

      2. Down'
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 2
  - slideName: Slide 17
    slideType: 2
    bodyText: Can black ladder the highlighted white stones successfully? Careful,
      this one's tricky!
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 0
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 18
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Correct! Even though the other white stones may seem far, black still
      bumps into one at the seventh move and gets put in Atari.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 0
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 19
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: You learned your first capture technique this lesson, great job! Come
      back next time for another one!
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
